--- concurrent -- concurrency primitives for the handl runtime.
---
--- Provides spawn/await/yield scheduling, synchronization primitives
--- (channels, mutexes, rwlocks, semaphores), atomics, cancellation
--- tokens, and basic TCP I/O -- all exposed as host functions backed
--- by swappable runtime backends.
---
--- ## scheduling
--- concurrent.spawn -- spawn a task from a function value, returning a task handle.
--- concurrent.await -- await a task, returning its result value.
--- concurrent.yield -- yield control to the scheduler, allowing other tasks to run.
--- concurrent.sleep -- sleep for a given number of milliseconds.
--- concurrent.timeout -- await a task with a timeout in milliseconds.
--- concurrent.may -- alias for spawn: fire-and-forget a task.
--- concurrent.must -- alias for timeout: await with a deadline.
--- concurrent.when -- alias for select: wait on the first available channel.
---
--- ## synchronization -- channels
--- concurrent.channel -- create a channel with an optional bounded capacity.
--- concurrent.send -- send a value on a channel (blocks if full).
--- concurrent.try_send -- try to send a value on a channel (errors if full).
--- concurrent.recv -- receive a value from a channel (blocks if empty).
--- concurrent.select -- wait on the first available value across an array of channels.
---
--- ## synchronization -- mutex
--- concurrent.mutex -- create a mutex.
--- concurrent.lock -- lock a mutex and run a thunk, then unlock.
--- concurrent.try_lock -- try to lock a mutex and run a thunk.
--- concurrent.unlock -- unlock a mutex.
---
--- ## synchronization -- rwlock
--- concurrent.rwlock -- create a read-write lock.
--- concurrent.read_lock -- acquire a read lock and run a thunk.
--- concurrent.write_lock -- acquire a write lock and run a thunk.
---
--- ## synchronization -- semaphore
--- concurrent.semaphore -- create a semaphore with a given permit count.
--- concurrent.acquire -- acquire permits from a semaphore (blocks if insufficient).
--- concurrent.try_acquire -- try to acquire permits (errors if insufficient).
--- concurrent.release -- release permits back to a semaphore.
---
--- ## atomics
--- concurrent.atomic -- create an atomic cell with an initial value.
--- concurrent.atomic_read -- read the current value of an atomic cell.
--- concurrent.atomic_write -- write a new value to an atomic cell, returning the old value.
--- concurrent.atomic_cas -- compare-and-swap on an atomic cell.
---
--- ## cancellation
--- concurrent.cancel_token -- create a cancellation token.
--- concurrent.cancel -- cancel a cancellation token.
--- concurrent.cancelable -- spawn a cancelable task tied to a cancellation token.
---
--- ## TCP I/O
--- concurrent.tcp_connect -- connect to a TCP address, returning a connection handle.
--- concurrent.tcp_send -- send data on a TCP connection.
--- concurrent.tcp_recv -- receive data from a TCP connection.
--- concurrent.tcp_close -- close a TCP connection.
